            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "A 3-way light switch allows you to control a light source from two separate points.<ref>https://www.homeimprovementweb.com/information/how-to/three-way-switch.htm</ref> Although a 3 way is one of the hardest electrical circuits to figure out, it's also one of the most useful.",
                    "#Understand non-metallic cables. NM (also called \"Romex®\") and UF (\"underground feeder\") cables both have plastic jacket wrapped around 2 (or more) insulated wires - including one white and one black - and a single uninsulated wire.<ref>https://www.homedepot.com/c/factors_to_consider_when_wiring_your_home_HT_BG_EL</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.first.gif}}"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "A 3-way light switch allows you to control a light source from two separate points.<ref>http://www.homeimprovementweb.com/information/how-to/three-way-switch.htm</ref> Although a 3 way is one of the hardest electrical circuits to figure out, it's also one of the most useful.",
                    "#Understand non-metallic cables. NM (also called \"Romex®\") and UF (\"underground feeder\") cables both have plastic jacket wrapped around 2 (or more) insulated wires - including one white and one black - and a single uninsulated wire.<ref>http://www.homedepot.com/c/factors_to_consider_when_wiring_your_home_HT_BG_EL</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 33.360p.first.gif}}"
                ]
            }
        },
