        {
            "id": "30038938",
            "user": "Seymour Edits",
            "timestamp": "18:39, 5 November 2021",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(29,752 bytes)",
            "change": 0,
            "summary": "(Fixing typo.)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "cleanup",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Connect ground wires, which is usually green.<ref>[v161932_b01]. 7 September 2021.</ref> Provide as shorter lengths (8 inches/20.5 cm) of bare or green insulated wire to this wire-nutted group to allow connection to green ground terminal screws on each device in the box (switches, outlets, fixtures, etc.) - one length of insulated wire per ground terminal screw. If the switch or junction box is metal, it too ''must be securely grounded'' with a green ground screw or approved grounding clip.  This must be done at each and every box that a cable enters and at each device that provides a termination point for ground.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.first.gif}}"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Connect ground wires, which if usually green.<ref>[v161932_b01]. 7 September 2021.</ref> Provide as shorter lengths (8 inches/20.5 cm) of bare or green insulated wire to this wire-nutted group to allow connection to green ground terminal screws on each device in the box (switches, outlets, fixtures, etc.) - one length of insulated wire per ground terminal screw. If the switch or junction box is metal, it too ''must be securely grounded'' with a green ground screw or approved grounding clip.  This must be done at each and every box that a cable enters and at each device that provides a termination point for ground.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.first.gif}}"
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "29885468",
            "user": "Seymour Edits",
            "timestamp": "18:12, 14 September 2021",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(29,752 bytes)",
            "change": 152,
            "summary": "(Added expert citations.)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Flip off power in the room you're working.<ref>[v161932_b01]. 7 September 2021.</ref> Head to your fuse box and make sure there is no power coming to the room you're currently working in. Use a voltage detector to ensure that you're not going to shock yourself once you start working.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1 Version 3.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.first.gif}}",
                    "#Connect ground wires, which if usually green.<ref>[v161932_b01]. 7 September 2021.</ref> Provide as shorter lengths (8 inches/20.5 cm) of bare or green insulated wire to this wire-nutted group to allow connection to green ground terminal screws on each device in the box (switches, outlets, fixtures, etc.) - one length of insulated wire per ground terminal screw. If the switch or junction box is metal, it too ''must be securely grounded'' with a green ground screw or approved grounding clip.  This must be done at each and every box that a cable enters and at each device that provides a termination point for ground.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.first.gif}}",
                    "#Connect 3 wire cable in the second switch box to the switch.  Connect all ground wires as previously described, if not already completed. Connect the black insulated wire to the shunt or common terminal screw of the switch (once again, the common screw terminal is the different colored screw from the rest of those on the switch).<ref>[v161932_b01]. 7 September 2021.</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.first.gif}}"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Flip off power in the room you're working. Head to your fuse box and make sure there is no power coming to the room you're currently working in. Use a voltage detector to ensure that you're not going to shock yourself once you start working.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1 Version 3.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 1.360p.first.gif}}",
                    "#Connect ground wires.  Provide as shorter lengths (8 inches/20.5 cm) of bare or green insulated wire to this wire-nutted group to allow connection to green ground terminal screws on each device in the box (switches, outlets, fixtures, etc.) - one length of insulated wire per ground terminal screw. If the switch or junction box is metal, it too ''must be securely grounded'' with a green ground screw or approved grounding clip.  This must be done at each and every box that a cable enters and at each device that provides a termination point for ground.<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 26.360p.first.gif}}",
                    "#Connect 3 wire cable in the second switch box to the switch.  Connect all ground wires as previously described, if not already completed. Connect the black insulated wire to the shunt or common terminal screw of the switch (once again, the common screw terminal is the different colored screw from the rest of those on the switch).<br><br>{{whvid|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.mp4|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30-preview.jpg|Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.jpg|gif=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.gif|giffirst=Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 30.360p.first.gif}}"
                ]
            }
        },
