                "added": [
                    "*It is not necessary to use #12 wire branching from an existing #14 wire circuit.  Number 12 gauge is required by code for kitchen and dining room receptacles, and other appliances (washers, refrigerators, etc.) that require 20A service (some bathrooms are wired with #12 to support hair dryers, etc., but is not a requirement)."
