                    "#Install a 3 wire cable from the first switch box to the light fixture's box.  Leave 8 - 10 inches of wire inside each of the boxes before cutting the cable to facilitate easy splicing and connection to the switch and fixture.  A 3 wire cable has an \"extra\" wire when compared to 2 wire cables, and this wire is nearly always covered in red insulation.  This third wire is necessary for 3-way switch installations.<br><br>[[Image:Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 5 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]"
