                    "#[[Image:Wire a 3 Way Light Switch Step 8.jpg|right|300px]]Connect feed wires in the first switch box. The 2 wire cable 'feed' from the power source enters the bottom of the switch box and the hot (black) wire connects to the common or shunt terminal on the 3-way switch.  This terminal is usually identified by a different color terminal screw (often darker) from the other two terminal screws (and the green ground screw).  In the picture of the circuit above, these terminals are on the lower right side of the switches.",
