                "removed": [
                    "#[[Image:Greenhex.jpg|right|184px|thumb|A couple of #10-32 green, hex head machine screws for electrical boxes.  The code has maintained that the ground connection be maintained separately from screws or other fasteners used to secure or support the electrical box in position.]][[Image:Ground4sq.jpg|right|184px|thumb|A green, hex head #10-32 machine screw designed expressly for the connection of a ground wire; installed into the factory threaded hole of a 4\" square box.]]Connect ground wires.  All ground wires in any box or enclosure must be connected together by wire nut, lug or other approved method.  Provide as many shorter lengths (8 inch) of bare or green insulated wire as needed to this wire nut group to allow connections to green ground terminal screws on each device in the box (switches, outlets, fixtures, etc.) and if the box is metal, it too must be grounded with a green ground screw or approved clip.  No connection is made to plastic or fiber boxes.  This must be done at each and every box and device that the cable enters or connects.  It is highly suggested that these ground connection be made first, then folded into the rear of the box - out of the way - leaving only the short ground leads out for easy connection to devices."
